  "Acrocanthosaurus": [
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "Content::2951306209",
      "Source": "Common Name: Acrocanthosaurus\r\nSpecies: Acrocanthosaurus Aegis\r\nTime: Early Cretaceous \r\nDiet: Carnivore \r\nTemperament: Aggressive\r\n\r\nAppearing much larger than expected, Acrocanthosaurus is a fearsom carnivorous theropod that makes even Rex look small. While doing slightly less damage than the fearsom Rex, Acro's gargantuan stature make their attacks particularly lethal against smaller opponents. When suffering from significant wounds in battle, Acro resort to using the massive flanks of their body as a sort of shield, mitigating the damage they recieve considerably. This \"shield stance\" can rapidly lead to Acro entering a state of adrenaline... so be careful. This rush of adrenaline will make an Acro frighteningly fast and extremely dangerous.\r\n\r\nAcrocanthosaurus appear to be immune to the typical method of applying narcotics. I have met few survivors which have managed to tame these beasts however, and they claim you can knockout an Acro by forcing narcotics down its throat as it gains its rush of adrenaline... no thank you... That being said, I have no doubt a tamed Acrocanthosaurus would prove very useful in combat, if its tanking and adrenaline can be utilized properly.\r\n",
      "Trans": {"SC":"","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":""}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "GraphLiteral::2634388422",
